---
/**
 * WhyLessCostSection.astro
 *
 * Educational section explaining the hospital billing gap vs USRad pricing.
 * Placed between SocialProofBar and HowItWorksSection on the homepage.
 */
---

<section class="pt-24 pb-28 px-4 sm:px-6 bg-gray-50">
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto">
    <div class="text-center mb-14">
      <h2 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">
        Why imaging through USRad costs less
      </h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        The scan is the same. The difference is how it's billed.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-16">
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900 mb-3">
          Hospitals bill through complex systems
        </h3>
        <p class="text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
          Hospitals bundle imaging into large billing systems and insurance
          networks, which often results in prices of $2,000–$5,000 for routine
          scans.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900 mb-3">
          Imaging centers specialize in scans
        </h3>
        <p class="text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
          Freestanding imaging centers focus only on diagnostic imaging. Without
          hospital overhead, they can perform the same scans far more
          efficiently.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900 mb-3">
          USRad connects you directly
        </h3>
        <p class="text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
          USRad routes patients to accredited imaging centers with transparent,
          all-inclusive pricing — typically 60–70% lower than hospital rates.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
